704
00:37:12,241 --> 00:37:16,440
The filling in more than half of Mikowaya's 40 different pastries

705
00:37:16,441 --> 00:37:19,240
is a paste made from azuki beans.

706
00:37:19,241 --> 00:37:23,780
The basic filling for Japanese pastries is anko,

707
00:37:23,781 --> 00:37:26,180
which is made from azuki bean.

708
00:37:26,181 --> 00:37:29,800
We have different pastries that uses the whole bean,

709
00:37:29,801 --> 00:37:32,800
which is called tsubushi-an.

710
00:37:32,801 --> 00:37:38,500
And then we have pastries that use just a string form of azuki,

711
00:37:38,501 --> 00:37:41,400
