740
00:39:25,140 --> 00:39:28,560
to the little red bean called azuki.

741
00:39:33,160 --> 00:39:36,100
It doesn't matter how sweet they taste.

742
00:39:36,101 --> 00:39:38,800
beans have one significant downside.

743
00:39:38,900 --> 00:39:41,000
It's the gas.

744
00:39:41,100 --> 00:39:45,440
And we don't mean biofuel.

745
00:39:45,540 --> 00:39:47,940
In the United States, it's a Southern tradition

746
00:39:48,040 --> 00:39:50,340
to eat black-eyed peas on New Year's Day

747
00:39:50,440 --> 00:39:52,720
to bring luck for the rest of the year.

748
00:39:52,820 --> 00:39:55,720
In Japan, roasted soybeans are thrown around homes

749
00:39:55,820 --> 00:39:57,880
on the eve of their first day of spring

750
00:39:57,980 --> 00:39:59,420
to ward off evil spirits.

751
00:39:59,421 --> 00:40:02,660
While the consumption of beans on a regular basis

752
00:40:02,661 --> 00:40:07,420
can reduce the risk of diabetes, heart disease, cancer,

753
00:40:07,421 --> 00:40:12,420
and obesity, there is that downside.

754
00:40:12,421 --> 00:40:14,420
Oh, yes, the flatulence problem.

755
00:40:14,421 --> 00:40:16,420
We hear questions about that often.

756
00:40:16,421 --> 00:40:19,420
So why do beans cause gas in the first place?

757
00:40:19,421 --> 00:40:21,420
The bean contains fiber and a lot

758
00:40:21,421 --> 00:40:25,420
of other complex materials, in particular, raffinose.

759
00:40:25,421 --> 00:40:27,760
and a lot of other complex materials,

760
00:40:27,860 --> 00:40:31,200
in particular, raffinose, which is a complex carbohydrate

761
00:40:31,201 --> 00:40:34,880
that is made up of three very simple components of sugar.

762
00:40:36,040 --> 00:40:39,140
As beans break down and pass through your digestive system,

763
00:40:39,820 --> 00:40:42,540
the small intestine extracts many of the bean's nutrients.

764
00:40:44,720 --> 00:40:47,280
But some of the complex carbohydrates in beans

765
00:40:47,281 --> 00:40:49,480
are too large for the small intestine to absorb,

766
00:40:49,900 --> 00:40:51,800
so they pass on to the large intestine.

767
00:40:51,801 --> 00:40:54,800
There's a lot of healthy bacteria there,

768
00:40:54,900 --> 00:40:57,040
which then act on those carbohydrates,

769
00:40:57,140 --> 00:40:58,300
breaking them down.

770
00:40:58,400 --> 00:41:01,540
It's in the process of breaking down these carbohydrates

771
00:41:01,640 --> 00:41:03,040
that gas is produced.

772
00:41:03,140 --> 00:41:08,380
And the gas can range everything from carbon dioxide, hydrogen,

